    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0298" n="1052" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1052"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/75</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-17T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7460. Your 5522, October 2, 6 p.m. Foreign Office state that British Ambassador,
                    Washington, has been authorized to issue letter of assurance regarding
                    consignment rye from United States to Sweden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
